WEBVTT

NOTE Why is the rate negative? English captions.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.755
The graph tracks distance remaining,
not distance already traveled.

2
00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.619
At first, six meters remain.

3
00:00:08.169 --> 00:00:10.958
Four seconds later, three meters remain.

4
00:00:11.908 --> 00:00:16.409
The change in remaining distance is
three minus six: negative three meters.

5
00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.690
Divide by four elapsed seconds to get

6
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.044
negative three-fourths
of a meter per second.

7
00:00:23.294 --> 00:00:27.028
For a move right four on
the graph, move down three.

8
00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:31.009
The negative sign describes
the decrease in what remains.
